    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d440">

                <pb facs="0769" n="699" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg699"/>

                <head>No 439.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Cayetano
                            Romero.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-09-15"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 15,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 16th ultimo, relative to the return of the articles stolen
                    from Mexican citizens by the Indians whom General Crook recently surprised and
                    captured in the Sierra Madre, and the formal agreement suggested by you to meet
                    such cases in the future.</p>
                <p>Adding that the matter will receive the attention of this Government,</p>
                <p>I avail, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
